  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CELAM/DEJUSOL Global Plan 2015-2019: Towards a Church which Goes Forth</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As the Latin American Episcopal Conference (CELAM) begins work under its new Global Plan 2015-2019, this project aims to support implementation of the objectives set for the Justice and Solidarity Department (DEJUSOL). The main goals of the Global Plan 2015-2019, developed against the backdrop of the 60th anniversary of the creation of CELAM, stress the intention to encourage &#x201C;a church which goes forth&#x201D;, that would be &#x201C;poor and for the poor&#x201D;. 

In this four-year period DEJUSOL&#x2019;s work will focus on such themes as: integral human development, migrants, refugees and displaced people, human trafficking, human rights, integral ecology, peace and reconciliation, health, children, prison populations, workers, role of the lay people, CST and collaboration at the international level. 

This project is a continuation of a long-standing relationship between CAFOD and CELAM.</narrative>
  </description>
